{"name":"Hazelnut","hex":"#a8715a","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"hazelnut","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The fruit of the hazel, especially of species Corylus avellana, which is grown commercially.","A light tan color inspired by the color of hazelnut."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hazelnut"}],"entries":[{"title":"Hazelnut","blocks":[{"text":"The hazelnut is the fruit of the hazel tree and therefore includes any of the nuts deriving from species of the genus Corylus, especially the nuts of the species Corylus avellana. They are also known as cobnuts or filberts according to species."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e4/Hazelnuts_%28Corylus_avellana%29_-_whole_with_kernels.jpg/330px-Hazelnuts_%28Corylus_avellana%29_-_whole_with_kernels.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hazelnut","wikidata":"Q578307"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/32/Haselnuss.jpg/500px-Haselnuss.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/32/Haselnuss.jpg/500px-Haselnuss.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Cracked hazelnut shell displaying the edible seed","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHaselnuss.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4c/Corylus_colurna_%281%29.JPG/500px-Corylus_colurna_%281%29.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4c/Corylus_colurna_%281%29.JPG/1280px-Corylus_colurna_%281%29.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4c/Corylus_colurna_%281%29.JPG/500px-Corylus_colurna_%281%29.JPG?utm_source=en.wikip